From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Belousov <michael.belousov98@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:14:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] web: precise render targets

The web backend implements Backend.support_precise_targets: a target created with
precision = .high is RGBA16F, which WebGL2 samples with linear filtering as standard
and renders into with EXT_color_buffer_float (or the half-float one). web.js checks
for the extension at context creation, and the first such framebuffer for
completeness, falling back to the 8-bit target where either fails. BlurBackdrop's
pyramid is the user: at 8 bits, its downsampled levels band.
---
 src/backends/web.js  | 165 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------
 src/backends/web.zig |  14 +++-
 2 files changed, 113 insertions(+), 66 deletions(-)

